commit_template_hash: 686bd6f6d3f60a9716f8ca85195b61c4852e2e6d8a91cf7a01fc867d6252a9af
intent: Fix nool_try arm: a Claude Code CLI 'rate_limit_event' telemetry line (status=allowed, routine on every session) was naively substring-matched as a real throttling incident, aborting the ticket -- and for the loop-based dispatch functions (run_footprint_gated, _lease_gated_dispatch), the aborted ticket's inflight entry never got removed, hanging the dispatch loop forever with zero CPU (verified: this is exactly what hung today's nool_try smoke test for 40+ minutes). transcript_rate_limited now parses rate_limit_event lines and only flags a non-allowed status; dropped the free-text 'session limit' marker (false-positives on ordinary English about app sessions/limits). Both dispatch loops now clean up inflight/leases on abort and stop admitting new work once aborted, instead of spinning. Also fixed a second correctness bug: nool_try's shared agent prompt told agents to land work via a git commit, but propose --try-branch --all only sees uncommitted changes -- every real ticket was landing 0% of the time (git commit succeeds, propose then finds nothing). Added a dedicated PROMPT_TRY telling the agent to leave changes uncommitted. Validated with real claude-sonnet-5 runs: single-ticket 1/1 accepted, full v1 8-ticket corpus 8/8 accepted zero conflicts (wall 81s, cost $0.87) -- first successful real-LLM run of the nool_try arm
knot_id: 59c7103e7a98bee1a3dc7fc8db75f245a9ae7835e969c45591a89127dedb809d
